{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>אפס ('however / only').</b> The sense: know that this which I have commanded you, that you shall not press your brother, is unnecessary if all Israel or most of them obey the voice of HaShem — then there will be no pauper among you who needs you to lend him. Rather, you shall lend to many nations — the sense is: you shall take his עבוט, which is a pledge, in exchange for money that you give him, which he needs in order to trade with it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:28.887809909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}